Create users (each one triggers an internal gRPC call to notification-service):

curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8080/users \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"name": "Shashank", "email": "shashank@example.com"}' | jq

curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8080/users \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"name": "Priya", "email": "priya@example.com"}' | jq


Get a user:

curl -s http://localhost:8080/users/user-1 | jq

Get notifications (proves the internal gRPC call from user-service → notification-service worked):

curl -s http://localhost:8080/notifications/user-1 | jq

Copy
bash
The jq at the end is optional — just pretty-prints the JSON. Remove it if you don't have jq installed.